      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren%2C_Rhode_Island",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Brown University began in Warren in 1764 as the College in the English Colony of Rhode Island and Providence Plantations.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren%2C_Rhode_Island",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The town sits on the former Wampanoag settlement of Sowams, a Pokanoket peninsula visited by Plymouth colonists in 1621.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        29,
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
